## 9. Design Quality Standards

La-Z-Boy's aesthetic direction: **luxury editorial** — clean but warm, confident whitespace, dramatic type scale, atmospheric depth. Every output should feel crafted, not templated.

### Shadows & Depth

Use brand-colored shadows, never generic gray — this creates cohesive branded depth:

```css
/* Always use these variables from Section 3 */
box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
/* on hover: */
box-shadow: var(--shadow-card-hover);
transform: translateY(-3px);
transition: box-shadow 250ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
            transform 250ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
```

### Backgrounds & Atmosphere

- Hero/dark sections: use gradients — `background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1B3A6B, #152f58, #0f2140)`
- Subtle noise/grain at 2–4% opacity adds tactile warmth
- Dot grids or geometric patterns at 3–6% opacity create depth
- Glass-morphism with `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)` works well for overlays on dark backgrounds

### Layout & Spacing

- **Asymmetric hero layouts**: text left, visual right — not centered text blocks
- **Generous spacing**: `padding: 80px 0` (or `py-20`) for sections — comfort brand should breathe
- **Decorative accents**: thin gradient bar at card tops, angled `clip-path` edges
- **Grid-breaking moments**: hero card spanning 2 columns, or offset positioning

### Motion & Animation

```css
/* Page load — staggered cascade */
.card:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 0ms; }
.card:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 100ms; }
.card:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 200ms; }

/* All interactive state changes need transition */
.interactive {
  transition: all 250ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
}

/* Hover lift */
.card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-3px);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card-hover);
}
```

Match animation complexity to context — internal tools need subtle polish, not pyrotechnics.

