## 10. Brand Voice & Tone

- **Warm and inviting** — every touchpoint should feel like sinking into a favorite chair
- **Comfortable, not casual** — professional but never stiff or corporate
- **Nostalgic yet modern** — rooted in 1927 heritage, forward-looking in experience
- **Calm and unhurried** — avoid urgency language, excessive punctuation, pushy sales tone

**Prefer**: comfort, ease, quality, crafted, lasting, home, warmth
**Avoid**: revolutionary, disruptive, best-in-class, synergy, leverage

---

## 11. What NOT to Do

- Never hardcode hex values — always use CSS variables or tokens
- Never use `#FFFFFF` as a page/slide background — use Warm White `#FAF8F5`
- Never use a font other than Helvetica Neue (or approved fallbacks)
- Never recreate the logo in CSS, SVG, or code — always use the official asset
- Never distort, recolor, or add effects to the wordmark
- Never use the tagline in any form other than `Live life comfortably.®`
- Never use Burnt Vermilion + Soft Celadon as the dominant color pair — too much contrast
- Never use Soft Celadon for body text — fails WCAG AA on white backgrounds
- Never use legacy La-Z-Boy Red `#CC0000` for new work — use Burnt Vermilion `#C0392B`
- Never use Burnt Vermilion as a background color
- Never use generic gray shadows `rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` — use brand-colored shadows
- Never use flat solid colors for hero backgrounds — use gradients within the palette
